================================================================================
MEDIA ASSETS ARE NOT PART OF THE MIT GRANT
================================================================================

The MIT permission above covers the SOFTWARE — the code and its documentation.

It does NOT cover the media assets. The video clips in `assets/videos/` and
`assets/screensaver/` are the author's own original animation artwork. All rights
to them are reserved by the author.

What you MAY do with the media assets:

  - Use them as they are, inside this plugin, for personal and non-commercial use.
  - Keep them in place when you fork the repository, so the plugin still works
    out of the box for you and for anyone else using it non-commercially.
  - Replace or delete them — the plugin discovers whatever is in those
    directories, and an empty pool is a legitimate state (the screen falls back
    to its own background).

What you MAY NOT do with the media assets:

  - Sell them, license them, or otherwise transfer them for money.
  - Use them commercially, in whole or in part, in any product or service.
  - Extract them and redistribute them as standalone artwork, a stock library,
    a background/wallpaper pack, or as content for a generative model.
  - Claim authorship of them.

If you want to use these clips commercially, or ship them inside a commercial
product, you need the author's explicit written permission. Without it, remove
the media assets from your copy and supply your own footage.

The plugin icons in `assets/icon/` (`icon-40.png`, `icon-80.png`, `icon-160.png`)
are NOT covered by this reservation — they are part of the SOFTWARE and follow
the MIT terms above.

Nothing here restricts the SOFTWARE's MIT grant: you can still use, modify,
sublicense and sell the code itself. The reservation applies to the media files
only, and only those files.
